    "body": "> > `readyState` is initialized as `complete` according to [#current-document-readiness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#current-document-readiness) and doesn't change.\n> \n> I'm not sure this is true—https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#read-html:initialise-the-document-object creates a document with a current document readiness of \"loading\".\n\nOh that could be right. But how do we get from `window.open` or an iframe to `#initialise-the-document-object`?\n\nAfaik, `#window-open-steps` -> `#the-rules-for-choosing-a-navigable` -> `#creating-a-new-top-level-traversable` -> `#creating-a-new-auxiliary-browsing-context` -> `#creating-a-new-browsing-context` which creates a `Document` without stating `#current-document-readiness`",
